e body fluids that are already close to seawater salinity (osmoconformers), so the osmotic stress is much lower. They also have efficient salt-excreting gills. ### In short Marine mammals don't drink seawater because it would **cost them water** rather than provide it. Their food and metabolism give them all the water they need, so evolution never favored developing a way to safely drink the sea. The fact that other animals (turtles, crabs, fish) *can* drink it just highlights how many different solutions exist to the same problem.
